1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:02,837
HI, YOU GUYS.
HI.

2
00:00:02,837 --> 00:00:04,755
WHAT'S THE MATTER?
WELL, IT'S JUST...

3
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:06,340
IT'S ONE OF THESE
SITUATIONS

4
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,925
THAT I JUST HATE.

5
00:00:07,925 --> 00:00:10,177
YOU KNOW, A MASSAGE CLIENT
GAVE ME THREE TICKETS

6
00:00:10,177 --> 00:00:13,012
TO THE HELMUT PELTZ EXHIBIT
AT THE MORGAN-CHASE MUSEUM.

7
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:15,975
NOW YOU'RE THINKING
YOU'VE GOT TO SLEEP WITH HIM.

8
00:00:15,975 --> 00:00:18,936
NO. NO, IT'S JUST THAT
HE GAVE ME THREE TICKETS

9
00:00:18,936 --> 00:00:20,771
AND THERE ARE SIX OF US.

10
00:00:20,771 --> 00:00:23,357
I'LL GIVE UP
MY TICKET.
ME, TOO.

11
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:25,484
OKAY. THAT'S SO GENEROUS.

12
00:00:25,484 --> 00:00:28,654
AND I THINK ROSS
IS GENEROUS, TOO.

13
00:00:28,654 --> 00:00:31,072
GREAT. OKAY,
THEN IT'S JUST US GIRLS.

14
00:00:31,072 --> 00:00:33,993
GREAT.
GREAT.

15
00:00:33,993 --> 00:00:36,578
SO WHAT-WHAT IS
THE EXHIBIT?

16
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:39,707
IT'S MOSTLY JUST PHOTOGRAPHS
OF, UM, LESBIAN LOVE SCENES

17
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:43,418
INTERSPERSED WITH VIDEO GAMES
AND FREE SANDWICHES.

18
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:48,924
OH, MAN...

19
00:00:52,051 --> 00:00:53,136
HEY.

20
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:54,221
HI THERE.
HEY.

21
00:00:54,221 --> 00:00:55,723
HEY, ROSS, LISTEN--

22
00:00:55,723 --> 00:00:57,056
CHANDLER GOT YOU OUT OF GOING

23
00:00:57,056 --> 00:00:59,184
TO THE LESBIAN/SANDWICH MUSEUM
THIS WEEKEND.

24
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:04,023
THANKS, BUT I HAVE PLANS.

25
00:01:04,023 --> 00:01:06,567
UH, ELIZABETH AND I
ARE GOING OUT OF TOWN.

26
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:08,527
OH, THAT'S GREAT--
THINK ABOUT ALL THE MONEY

27
00:01:08,527 --> 00:01:10,070
THAT YOU'RE GOING TO MAKE.

28
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,780
WHY? WHAT?

29
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:15,075
WELL, HER FATHER PAYS YOU
FOR BABY-SITTING, RIGHT?

30
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:18,662
NO. THAT'S FUNNY, BUT MAYBE
IT'S TIME TO MOVE ON

31
00:01:18,662 --> 00:01:22,332
YOU KNOW, LET IT GO, STOP IT.

32
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:24,960
BESIDES, RACHEL'S GOING OUT
WITH ELIZABETH'S FATHER

33
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:27,629
SO, UH, HE'S MUCH
OLDER THAN SHE IS.

34
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:33,343
LOOKS LIKE I'M NOT THE ONLY ONE
INTERESTED IN FOSSILS, HUH?

35
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:35,345
ROSS, ALL THAT DOES
IS REMIND US

36
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:37,347
THAT YOU ARE INTERESTED
IN FOSSILS.

37
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:41,560
OKAY, OKAY.
UH, WELL, UH

38
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:46,565
RACHEL'S GOING TO NEED TO
YELLSWEET NOTHING'S
IN HIS EAR, HUH?

39
00:01:48,692 --> 00:01:49,777
ROSS...

40
00:01:49,777 --> 00:01:51,653
OH, COME ON,
YOU GUYS

41
00:01:51,653 --> 00:01:53,405
THAT'S FUNNY, YOU KNOW,
'CAUSE HE'S GOING TO...

42
00:01:53,405 --> 00:01:55,657
HE'S GOT, LIKE, A HEARING AID,
YOU KNOW, 'CAUSE...

43
00:01:55,657 --> 00:01:57,200
OH...

44
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,869
'CAUSE HE'S ALL OLD, YOU KNOW?

45
00:01:58,869 --> 00:02:00,662
( Paul chuckling )

46
00:02:08,837 --> 00:02:11,548
'KAY, LOOK, ROSS...

47
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,050
JUST SO YOU KNOW,

48
00:02:13,050 --> 00:02:14,509
SINCE LIZZIE LIKES
YOU SO MUCH

49
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:15,844
I'VE DECIDED TO
ACCEPT THE FACT

50
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:17,387
THAT YOU'RE GOING
OUT WITH HER.

51
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:19,473
REALLY? THAT...
OKAY, THAT'S GREAT.

52
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:21,725
YEAH. BUT THEN I
CHANGED MY MIND.

53
00:02:21,725 --> 00:02:23,268
I'M FUNNY LIKE THAT.

54
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:25,562
SO I'VE TOLD LIZZIE

55
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:27,064
AND NOW I'M TELLING YOU--

56
00:02:27,064 --> 00:02:29,108
I DON'T WANT YOU SEEING
MY DAUGHTER ANYMORE.

57
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:32,193
ALL RIGHT, LOOK,
I-I REALIZE IT UPSETS YOU...

58
00:02:32,193 --> 00:02:33,487
YES, IT DOES.

59
00:02:35,447 --> 00:02:38,366
BUT... ELIZABETH AND I
ARE BOTH ADULTS

60
00:02:38,366 --> 00:02:42,871
AND SO I DON'T THINK
THERE'S REALLY ANYTHING
YOU CAN DO ABOUT IT.

61
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,665
I'LL CALL THE UNIVERSITY
AND TELL THEM ABOUT
YOUR RELATIONSHIP

62
00:02:44,665 --> 00:02:45,916
AND HAVE YOU FIRED.

63
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:47,960
OH! A MAN WITH A PLAN.

64
00:02:56,135 --> 00:03:01,306
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

65
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:03,558
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

66
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:05,894
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

67
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:10,899
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

68
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:13,360
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

69
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:16,571
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

70
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:19,825
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

71
00:03:19,825 --> 00:03:23,078
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

72
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:31,419
THIS IS SO EXCITING.

73
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:33,088
YOU GET YOUR PICTURE
BACK UP THERE

74
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:34,173
ON THE WALL OF FAME.

75
00:03:34,173 --> 00:03:35,465
I KNOW.

76
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:36,925
IT WAS SO COOL
WHEN I WAS UP THERE BEFORE.

77
00:03:36,925 --> 00:03:38,052
ME AND JIM BELUSHI
WOULD BE

78
00:03:38,052 --> 00:03:39,260
CRACKING UP
ABOUT SOMETHING.

79
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,262
THEN I GET FIRED

80
00:03:41,262 --> 00:03:42,931
OFF DAYS OF OUR LIVES

81
00:03:42,931 --> 00:03:44,599
AND HE TAKES ME DOWN.

82
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:46,768
NOW HE'S JUST
LAUGHING AT ME.

83
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:49,938
LOOK AT HIM, THAT
SMUG BELUSHI BASTARD.

84
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:53,984
OH, OKAY, MAYBE WHEN
THEY PUT YOUR PICTURE BACK UP

85
00:03:53,984 --> 00:03:57,112
THEY COULD PUT YOU
NEXT TO MATT LAUER.

86
00:03:57,112 --> 00:03:58,906
LOOK AT HIM JUST
SMILING AT ME.

87
00:03:58,906 --> 00:04:01,867
( giggles )

88
00:04:01,867 --> 00:04:05,037
YEAH, I KNOW,
WE'D BE GREAT TOGETHER.

89
00:04:05,037 --> 00:04:06,621
OH... PSST.

90
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:09,624
HEY. SO, I'M BACK.

91
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:11,626
( foreign accent ):
WHO ARE YOU?

92
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:14,922
JOEY TRIBBIANI.

93
00:04:14,922 --> 00:04:17,298
FROM THE WALL?

94
00:04:17,298 --> 00:04:21,762
OKAY, MAYBE THIS WILL
JOG YOUR MEMORY, HUH?

95
00:04:21,762 --> 00:04:23,889
HUH?

96
00:04:23,889 --> 00:04:26,767
OKAY, ANYWAY, I'M READY
TO GO BACK UP ON THE WALL.

97
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:28,435
I'M THE STAR
OF A NEW TV SHOW.

98
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:31,605
SHOW ME IN THE TV BOOK.

99
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:33,774
WELL, IT'S NOT
ON TV YET.

100
00:04:33,774 --> 00:04:36,110
WELL, THEN IT'S
NOT ON THE WALL YET.

101
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:42,116
OKAY, FINE.
I WILL BRING YOU A TAPE, HUH?

102
00:04:42,116 --> 00:04:43,658
SO, NOW, DO YOU HAVE

103
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:46,369
ANY OF MATT LAUER'S CLOTHES
HERE, MAYBE?

104
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:48,371
JUST ONES THAT HAVEN'T
BEEN CLEANED YET?

105
00:04:56,088 --> 00:04:57,089
I LOVE MUSEUMS.

106
00:04:57,089 --> 00:04:58,506
SOAKING UP ALL THE CULTURE.

107
00:04:58,506 --> 00:04:59,716
YEAH.

108
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:01,051
WHERE DO YOU WANT
TO START?

109
00:05:01,051 --> 00:05:02,719
OH, THE GIFT SHOP!

110
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:03,762
YEAH!

111
00:05:03,762 --> 00:05:05,013
HEY, AND THEN LUNCH.

112
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:06,098
OH, WAIT. YES

113
00:05:06,098 --> 00:05:07,599
BUT I CAN'T EAT TOO MUCH.

114
00:05:07,599 --> 00:05:08,976
PAUL'S TAKING ME OUT
TO DINNER TONIGHT.

115
00:05:08,976 --> 00:05:10,602
HE SAID HE HAS
A BIG SURPRISE PLANNED.

116
00:05:10,602 --> 00:05:13,438
OH, WOW. DO YOU THINK
MAYBE HE'S GOING

117
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:15,023
TO TELL YOU HE'S GAY?

118
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:17,609
WHAT? NO. WHY?

119
00:05:17,609 --> 00:05:19,027
NO REASON.

120
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:22,114
THAT WOULD JUST BE
A REALLY BIG SURPRISE, RIGHT?

121
00:05:22,114 --> 00:05:23,698
YOU CAN PUT THE
AISLE OVER HERE

122
00:05:23,698 --> 00:05:25,742
AND HAVE THE WEDDING
CEREMONY RIGHT OVER HERE.

123
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:27,661
I DIDN'T KNOW
YOU COULD GET
MARRIED HERE.

124
00:05:27,661 --> 00:05:29,746
THIS WOULD BE
A BEAUTIFUL PLACE
TO GET MARRIED.

125
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:31,456
BUT I WOULDN'T PUT
THE AISLE THERE

126
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:33,458
AND I WOULD NEVER
HAVE THE CEREMONY THERE.

127
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:36,461
YOU'D HAVE THE CEREMONY UNDER
THIS BIG BEAUTIFUL ARCH.

128
00:05:36,461 --> 00:05:37,462
MAY I HELP YOU?

129
00:05:37,462 --> 00:05:38,505
OH, SORRY.

130
00:05:38,505 --> 00:05:39,714
DIDN'T MEAN
TO INTERRUPT.

131
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:41,300
IT'S JUST SUCH
A BEAUTIFUL SPACE.

132
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,968
DO YOU DO A LOT
OF WEDDINGS HERE?

133
00:05:42,968 --> 00:05:44,719
YES, WE'RE VERY POPULAR.

134
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:48,182
THERE'S A TWO-YEAR
WAITING LIST. SORRY.

135
00:05:48,182 --> 00:05:49,474
MONICA, YOU SHOULD

136
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:50,976
TOTALLY PUT YOUR NAME DOWN
FOR THIS PLACE.

137
00:05:50,976 --> 00:05:52,644
WHAT? ARE YOU CRAZY?

138
00:05:52,644 --> 00:05:54,729
I'M NOT GETTING MARRIED.

139
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:56,315
I'M NOT EVEN ENGAGED.

140
00:05:56,315 --> 00:05:57,732
BUT THERE'S A TWO-YEAR WAIT

141
00:05:57,732 --> 00:05:59,943
AND THEN WHAT IF
YOU GET ENGAGED
IN TWO YEARS

142
00:05:59,943 --> 00:06:02,279
AND THEN YOU'VE GOT
TO WAIT ANOTHER TWO
YEARS FOR THIS PLACE?

143
00:06:02,279 --> 00:06:03,822
THAT'S FOUR YEARS.

144
00:06:03,822 --> 00:06:05,699
CHANDLER'S NOT GOING
TO WAIT THAT LONG.

145
00:06:05,699 --> 00:06:07,868
HE'S GOING TO FIND
SOMEBODY ELSE, YOU KNOW?

146
00:06:07,868 --> 00:06:08,869
SOMEONE WHO DID PUT

147
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:10,620
THEIR NAME
ON THE LIST.

148
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,747
AND IT CAN'T HURT
TO PUT YOUR NAME DOWN.

149
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:14,333
IF IN TWO YEARS
YOU'RE NOT ENGAGED

150
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:16,001
YOU JUST DON'T USE IT.

151
00:06:16,001 --> 00:06:20,297
WELL, I GUESS THERE IS NO HARM
IN PUTTING MY NAME DOWN.

152
00:06:20,297 --> 00:06:21,798
I'M GOING
TO DO IT, TOO.

153
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:23,717
ME, TOO.

154
00:06:23,717 --> 00:06:25,384
REALLY? WHO WOULD
YOU MARRY?

155
00:06:25,384 --> 00:06:26,928
I DON'T KNOW.

156
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:28,263
I DON'T HAVE ANYONE
RIGHT NOW, YOU KNOW?

157
00:06:28,263 --> 00:06:29,388
OH, PHEEBS.

158
00:06:29,388 --> 00:06:31,099
DON'T FEEL TOO SORRY FOR ME.

159
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:32,767
AT LEAST MY BOYFRIEND ISN'T GAY.

160
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:36,395
PHOEBE, THAT'S NOT...

161
00:06:36,395 --> 00:06:38,606
DON'T EVEN GET ME
STARTED ON YOURS.

162
00:06:40,441 --> 00:06:41,651
HEY.

163
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:43,402
SO, DID YOU WATCH
THE TAPE OF MY SHOW?

164
00:06:43,402 --> 00:06:44,779
I DID.

165
00:06:44,779 --> 00:06:46,907
ALL RIGHT. LET'S GET ME
BACK UP THERE.

166
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:48,825
NO, YOU DON'T GO UP
ON THE WALL.

167
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:49,868
WHAT?

168
00:06:49,868 --> 00:06:51,703
BUT YOU SAW THE SHOW.

169
00:06:51,703 --> 00:06:54,373
YES. IT WAS VERY OFFENSIVE
TO MY PEOPLE.

170
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:58,085
DRY CLEANERS?

171
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:03,882
RUSSIANS. IT SHOWED THEM
AS TERRORISTS AND VILLAINS.

172
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:04,966
OKAY, OKAY, LOOK

173
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:06,551
YOU GOT HARRISON FORD
UP THERE.

174
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:07,886
THAT'S RIGHT.

175
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:09,971
MR. FORD IS
A VERY GOOD CUSTOMER.

176
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:11,390
HE BRINGS US A LOT OF CLOTHES.

177
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:12,431
YOU BRING US NOTHING.

178
00:07:12,431 --> 00:07:14,268
OKAY, WELL, THAT MAY BE TRUE

179
00:07:14,268 --> 00:07:17,604
BUT IN AIR FORCE ONE, OKAY,
THE RUSSIANS WERE TERRORISTS

180
00:07:17,604 --> 00:07:20,274
AND EVIL, AND PLUS HE KILLS
A BUNCH OF THEM.

181
00:07:20,274 --> 00:07:22,192
THAT'S OFFENSIVE TO RUSSIANS.

182
00:07:22,192 --> 00:07:23,484
I'VE NEVER SEEN IT.

183
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:25,279
OH, YOU SHOULD. IT'S GREAT.

184
00:07:31,076 --> 00:07:33,703
THIS PLACE IS REALLY BEAUTIFUL.

185
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:36,373
YEAH, I'VE BEEN COMING HERE
SINCE I WAS A KID.

186
00:07:36,373 --> 00:07:38,166
THIS USED TO BE MY GRANDMA'S.

187
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:41,753
WOW. THE ONLY THING I GOT
FROM MY GRANDMOTHER
WAS HER EYES.

188
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:45,215
I MEAN, NOT HER ACTUAL
EYEBALLS

189
00:07:45,215 --> 00:07:47,926
BUT PEOPLE SAY
THAT MY EYES...

190
00:07:47,926 --> 00:07:48,969
DO YOU WANT TO MAKE OUT?

191
00:07:48,969 --> 00:07:50,720
SURE.

192
00:07:52,306 --> 00:07:55,267
MM.

193
00:07:55,267 --> 00:07:57,144
ARE YOU OKAY?
WHAT'S WRONG?

194
00:07:57,144 --> 00:08:00,647
UH, I WAS JUST THINKING
ABOUT YOUR FATHER.

195
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:03,317
WELL, WHATEVER
WORKS FOR YOU.

196
00:08:03,317 --> 00:08:07,946
NO, NO. UH...

197
00:08:07,946 --> 00:08:10,698
HE JUST REALLY
FREAKED ME OUT BEFORE.

198
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:13,660
OH. WELL, SO WE HAVE
TO HIDE OUR RELATIONSHIP

199
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:16,496
FROM ONE MORE PERSON,
BIG DEAL.

200
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:18,748
BESIDES, WE'VE HAD
FUN HIDING IT.

201
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:20,708
YEAH.

202
00:08:21,876 --> 00:08:24,338
MM.

203
00:08:24,338 --> 00:08:27,090
HEY, UM, YOU BROUGHT
PROTECTION, RIGHT?

204
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:29,759
WHY? ARE THERE, LIKE,
BEARS OR SOMETHING?

205
00:08:29,759 --> 00:08:32,012
NO.

206
00:08:32,012 --> 00:08:33,888
OH. OH!

207
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:35,515
OH, PROTECTION.

208
00:08:35,515 --> 00:08:38,310
NO, YEAH.
NO, THAT-THAT I FORGOT.

209
00:08:38,310 --> 00:08:40,687
I'LL JUST RUN TO
THE STORE AND GET SOME.

210
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,230
NO, HEY, HEY,
I'M THE GUY.

211
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,315
I'LL GET IT.

212
00:08:43,315 --> 00:08:44,732
DO YOU KNOW WHERE
THE STORE IS?

213
00:08:44,732 --> 00:08:46,485
NO.

214
00:08:46,485 --> 00:08:48,028
DO YOU WANT TO RIDE
AROUND TOWN

215
00:08:48,028 --> 00:08:49,779
ON MY LITTLE PINK BICYCLE?

216
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:51,031
A LITTLE BIT.

217
00:08:51,031 --> 00:08:53,408
[LAUGHS]

218
00:08:53,408 --> 00:08:55,285
I'LL BE BACK
IN TEN MINUTES.
OKAY.

219
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:56,577
WHY DON'T YOU GET
IN THE HOT TUB

220
00:08:56,577 --> 00:08:58,079
AND I'LL MEET YOU THERE?

221
00:08:58,079 --> 00:08:59,498
OKAY.

222
00:09:11,301 --> 00:09:13,594
( door opens )

223
00:09:13,594 --> 00:09:16,348
Rachel:
OH, MY GOD,
WHAT A GREAT SURPRISE.

224
00:09:16,348 --> 00:09:18,141
THIS IS SUCH
A BEAUTIFUL HOUSE.

225
00:09:18,141 --> 00:09:20,435
Paul:
THANK YOU. IT USED
TO BE MY MOTHER'S.

226
00:09:20,435 --> 00:09:21,644
THIS IS THE KITCHEN.

227
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:27,734
( phone rings )

228
00:09:27,734 --> 00:09:29,986
Chandler:
You've reached Monica
and Chandler's.

229
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:33,114
If you're listening
to this message,
we're probably screening.

230
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:36,743
YEAH, WE ARE.
( machine beeps )

231
00:09:36,743 --> 00:09:39,704
Hi. This is Hildy
from the Morgan-Chase museum.

232
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:41,581
I'm calling for Monica Geller.

233
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:43,166
I want to let her know
that there was a cancellation

234
00:09:43,166 --> 00:09:45,168
and if she's still interested

235
00:09:45,168 --> 00:09:47,837
in having the Bing-Geller
wedding in our facility

236
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:49,589
it is available...

237
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:52,092
THIS IS CHANDLER BING!
THIS IS CHANDLER BING!

238
00:09:53,468 --> 00:09:56,179
YES, THE GROOM.
NO, NOT THE GROOM!

239
00:10:02,477 --> 00:10:05,146
SO SECLUDED
UP HERE.
I KNOW.

240
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:07,732
THAT'S WHY I LIKE IT HERE.

241
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:09,443
MM-HMM. I FEEL
LIKE WE'RE

242
00:10:09,443 --> 00:10:11,027
THE ONLY TWO PEOPLE
IN THE WORLD.

243
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:13,196
WHOOPS.

244
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:14,573
SORRY.

245
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:16,657
( gasps )

246
00:10:19,286 --> 00:10:21,121
WHAT'S THE MATTER, HONEY?

247
00:10:21,121 --> 00:10:22,539
DID YOU SEE A LITTLE MOUSE?

248
00:10:22,539 --> 00:10:23,706
NO, NO. BIG BEAR.

249
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:24,874
BIG BEAR OUTSIDE.

250
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:26,834
I THOUGHT I HEARD A BEAR.

251
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:28,253
WOULD YOU GO
CHECK ON THAT?

252
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:29,254
HONEY, WE DON'T HAVE

253
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:31,172
ANY BEARS HERE.

254
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:32,507
WELL, OKAY.

255
00:10:32,507 --> 00:10:34,968
W-WOULD YOU GET
ME A DIET COKE?

256
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:36,595
OKAY.

257
00:10:36,595 --> 00:10:38,930
BE RIGHT BACK.
OKAY.

258
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:39,889
OKAY.

259
00:10:42,641 --> 00:10:44,894
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

260
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:46,771
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?
I CAME WITH PAUL.

261
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:48,689
YEAH, I RECOGNIZE
THE ANKLES.

262
00:10:48,689 --> 00:10:49,941
GET OUT. GET OUT.

263
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:54,070
HERE YOU GO, HONEY.

264
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:56,072
OH, THANK YOU.

265
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,073
DIET COKE.

266
00:10:57,073 --> 00:10:58,950
OH... ICE.

267
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:01,369
I NEED ICE.

268
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:04,456
OKAY.

269
00:11:04,456 --> 00:11:06,166
THANK YOU.
BE RIGHT BACK.

270
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:07,125
OKAY.

271
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:10,253
YOU AND YOUR ICE.

272
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:12,713
OH! GET OUT!

273
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,591
GET OUT, GO. COME ON.

274
00:11:14,591 --> 00:11:16,510
QUICK.

275
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:18,386
NO, NOT IN THERE.
NOT IN THERE.

276
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:19,720
HE'S IN THERE.

277
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:22,015
DID YOU REALLY
HEAR A BEAR?

278
00:11:22,015 --> 00:11:22,974
GO!

279
00:11:26,436 --> 00:11:28,062
HERE YOU GO, HONEY.

280
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:30,106
OH!

281
00:11:30,106 --> 00:11:32,025
ONE DIET COKE
WITH ICE.

282
00:11:32,025 --> 00:11:33,818
OH, THANK YOU.

283
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:39,073
I AM... SO HAPPY
THAT YOU'RE HERE.

284
00:11:39,073 --> 00:11:40,074
HERE I AM!

285
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:41,368
ELIZABETH!

286
00:11:41,368 --> 00:11:43,244
OH, LOOK!
ELIZABETH'S HERE!

287
00:11:44,996 --> 00:11:47,666
WHO ARE YOU
TALKING TO?

288
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:51,002
YOU GUYS?

289
00:11:51,002 --> 00:11:53,004
HOW DID YOU KNOW
WE WERE HERE?

290
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:54,673
UM...

291
00:11:54,673 --> 00:11:57,300
WELL, SHE OBVIOUSLY
SAW THE TIRE TRACKS

292
00:11:57,300 --> 00:12:00,178
THAT WERE LEADING UP
TO THE CLOSED GARAGE.

293
00:12:00,178 --> 00:12:02,639
OBVIOUSLY.

294
00:12:02,639 --> 00:12:04,307
ELIZABETH...

295
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:07,018
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

296
00:12:12,566 --> 00:12:14,317
DID-DID-DID YOU
COME UP HERE

297
00:12:14,317 --> 00:12:16,903
TO WORK ON THAT TERM
PAPER OR SOMETHING?

298
00:12:16,903 --> 00:12:18,488
YEAH, YEAH.

299
00:12:18,488 --> 00:12:19,906
WELL, WHY DON'T
YOU, YOU KNOW

300
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:21,700
GO IN THAT ROOM AND
DO YOUR HOMEWORK?

301
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:24,077
OH, I WOULDN'T DO IT
IN THERE, UM

302
00:12:24,077 --> 00:12:25,662
THAT'S MY DAD'S BEDROOM.

303
00:12:27,706 --> 00:12:31,750
THAT'S YOUR...
THAT'S YOUR
DAD'S BEDROOM.

304
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:34,045
( loudly ):
THAT'S YOUR
DAD'S BEDROOM!

305
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:36,590
HO-HO!

306
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:38,299
WHY ARE YOU YELLING,
RACHEL?

307
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:40,677
THAT DIET COKE, I THINK--
JUST STRAIGHT TO MY HEAD.

308
00:12:40,677 --> 00:12:42,637
WHOO!

309
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:49,018
HI, HONEY.

310
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:50,103
SEE YA LATER.

311
00:12:51,354 --> 00:12:52,355
WHAT, I-I BOUGHT
GROCERIES.

312
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:53,898
I WAS GOING TO MAKE YOU DINNER.

313
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:55,233
WELL, NEXT TIME, ASK.

314
00:12:58,819 --> 00:13:00,988
OR, AT LEAST,
WAIT FOR ME TO ASK.

315
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,416
( beeps )

316
00:13:11,416 --> 00:13:13,876
Hi, this is Hildy
from the Morgan-Chase Museum.

317
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:15,670
I'm calling for Monica Geller.

318
00:13:15,670 --> 00:13:17,255
OH, NO.

319
00:13:17,255 --> 00:13:19,507
I want to let her know
that there was a cancellation

320
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:20,799
and if she's still interested

321
00:13:20,799 --> 00:13:22,218
in having
the Bing-Geller wedding

322
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:24,095
in our facility...

323
00:13:24,095 --> 00:13:25,430
OH, PLEASE.

324
00:13:25,430 --> 00:13:26,556
OH, PLEASE,
HE DIDN'T HEAR IT.

325
00:13:26,556 --> 00:13:27,890
HE DIDN'T HEAR IT!

326
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:29,934
This is Chandler Bing!
This is Chandler Bing!

327
00:13:31,728 --> 00:13:34,439
NO!

328
00:13:37,024 --> 00:13:38,067
CAN I HELP YOU?

329
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:39,402
UH... YEAH. WHERE'S THE GUY

330
00:13:39,402 --> 00:13:41,738
WHO DECIDES WHOSE PICTURES
GO UP ON THE WALL?

331
00:13:41,738 --> 00:13:43,531
HE'S NOT HERE RIGHT NOW.

332
00:13:43,531 --> 00:13:45,408
OH, YOU'RE KIDDING ME.

333
00:13:45,408 --> 00:13:47,577
ALL RIGHT, MAKE SURE YOU
TELL HIM THAT JOEY TRIBBIANI

334
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:50,997
STOPPED BY TO DROP OFF
ALL THESE CLOTHES. I'M AN ACTOR.

335
00:13:50,997 --> 00:13:52,707
I'M TRYING TO GET MY PICTURE
UP THERE ON THE WALL.

336
00:13:52,707 --> 00:13:54,875
YOU KNOW, THERE ARE TWO PEOPLE

337
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:57,378
WHO COULD GET YOUR PICTURE
UP THERE.

338
00:13:57,378 --> 00:13:59,380
OH, REALLY?

339
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:03,718
WELL, MAYBE YOU AND I
GO OUT FOR DRINKS.

340
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:05,804
YOU'RE THE OTHER ONE,
RIGHT?

341
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:11,726
SO, LIZZIE, ARE YOU
PLANNING ON STAYING THE NIGHT?

342
00:14:11,726 --> 00:14:13,353
OH, NO, NO.

343
00:14:13,353 --> 00:14:15,229
BELIEVE ME, I'M LEAVING
AS SOON AS POSSIBLE.

344
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:17,231
GOOD. GOOD.

345
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:19,400
NOT THAT WE DON'T
WANT YOU TO STAY.

346
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,027
OBVIOUSLY, YOU'RE WELCOME.

347
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:23,196
HOW MUCH MORE HOMEWORK
DO YOU HAVE?

348
00:14:23,196 --> 00:14:25,072
UH, I JUST HAVE ONE PROBLEM LEFT

349
00:14:25,072 --> 00:14:26,949
THAT I DO NOT KNOW HOW TO SOLVE.

350
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:29,452
UH, RACHEL,
MAYBE YOU WANT TO COME UPSTAIRS

351
00:14:29,452 --> 00:14:31,037
AND HELP ME FIGURE IT OUT?

352
00:14:31,037 --> 00:14:32,706
( shaky ):
REALLY?

353
00:14:32,706 --> 00:14:34,374
OKAY.

354
00:14:34,374 --> 00:14:36,835
OKAY, I-I'LL
GO UPSTAIRS...

355
00:14:36,835 --> 00:14:40,755
IF-IF YOU... GET ME
SOMETHING FROM THE CAR.

356
00:14:40,755 --> 00:14:43,508
WHAT DO YOU NEED
FROM THE CAR?

357
00:14:43,508 --> 00:14:45,259
SURPRISE ME.

358
00:14:48,346 --> 00:14:50,765
( yelling ):
SO, YOU'RE GOING TO BE
IN THE CAR

359
00:14:50,765 --> 00:14:52,225
I WILL BE UPSTAIRS

360
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:54,394
AND THAT'S WHERE EVERYBODY'S
GOING TO BE!

361
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:18,209
( heavy sigh )

362
00:15:18,209 --> 00:15:19,335
JUST RELAX, JUST RELAX.

363
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:20,628
PAUL, YOU'RE DOING GREAT.

364
00:15:20,628 --> 00:15:22,463
SHE LIKES YOU.

365
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:24,215
SHE...

366
00:15:24,215 --> 00:15:25,633
I THINK SHE LIKES YOU.

367
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:27,051
SHE LIKES YOU.

368
00:15:27,051 --> 00:15:28,052
YOU KNOW WHY?

369
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:29,095
BECAUSE YOU'RE A...

370
00:15:29,095 --> 00:15:31,138
NEAT GUY.

371
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:35,476
YOU ARE THE MAN.

372
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:37,812
YOU ARE THE MAN!

373
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:42,650
STILL GOT IT.

374
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,527
( inhaling )

375
00:15:44,527 --> 00:15:46,821
STILL SEXY.

376
00:15:46,821 --> 00:15:49,407
YOU'RE JUST A LOVE MACHINE.

377
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:51,910
( high-pitched ):
♪ I'M JUST A LOVE MACHINE ♪

378
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:54,913
♪ AND I DON'T WORK
FOR NOBODY BUT YOU ♪

379
00:15:54,913 --> 00:15:58,124
♪ YEAH, BABY, HUH! ♪

380
00:15:58,124 --> 00:16:00,877
( roaring )

381
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:07,174
SHOW TIME.

382
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:09,844
♪ I'M JUST A LOVE MACHINE ♪

383
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:11,095
♪ YEAH, BABY! ♪

384
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:12,847
♪ HUH! ♪

385
00:16:13,890 --> 00:16:15,642
PHOEBE...
YEAH?

386
00:16:15,642 --> 00:16:16,935
HAVE YOU SEEN
CHANDLER?

387
00:16:16,935 --> 00:16:18,269
NO, WHY?

388
00:16:18,269 --> 00:16:19,687
THE WOMAN FROM
THE MUSEUM CALLED

389
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:21,105
AND SAID THAT THERE
WAS A CANCELLATION

390
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,565
AND THAT WE COULD
MOVE UP OUR WEDDING

391
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:23,733
AND CHANDLER HEARD.

392
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:25,401
( gasps )
I KNOW.

393
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:26,861
HOW BAD IS THIS?

394
00:16:26,861 --> 00:16:29,196
WELL, WITH A REGULAR GUY,
IT'S BAD.

395
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:31,157
WITH CHANDLER--
OH, DEAR GOD!

396
00:16:31,157 --> 00:16:32,659
I KNOW, I KNOW.

397
00:16:32,659 --> 00:16:34,076
AND HE TOTALLY
FREAKED OUT

398
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:35,495
AND I CAN'T FIND
HIM ANYWHERE.

399
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:36,913
WHAT ARE YOU
GOING TO DO?

400
00:16:36,913 --> 00:16:38,331
I'M NEVER GOING
TO LISTEN TO YOU AGAIN

401
00:16:38,331 --> 00:16:39,833
THAT'S FOR SURE.

402
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:41,250
( whiny ):
AND WHAT HARM CAN IT DO

403
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,669
IF YOU JUST PUT YOUR NAME DOWN?

404
00:16:42,669 --> 00:16:44,462
RACHEL SAID THAT.

405
00:16:44,462 --> 00:16:45,546
WELL, RACHEL'S NOT HERE!

406
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:54,889
OH, HERE IT IS!

407
00:16:54,889 --> 00:16:57,892
OOH, JOEY, WHY DID YOU SIGN IT
"SON OF A BITCH"?

408
00:17:00,436 --> 00:17:01,646
I DIDN'T DO THAT.

409
00:17:01,646 --> 00:17:03,272
WHO WOULD'VE DONE THAT?

410
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:04,524
SON OF A BITCH!

411
00:17:04,524 --> 00:17:06,943
OKAY, MAYBE ASK THIS GUY.

412
00:17:06,943 --> 00:17:08,027
YOU--

413
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,445
GET OUT OF MY SHOP!

414
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:10,613
WHAT DID HE DO?

415
00:17:10,613 --> 00:17:11,739
HE WENT OUT WITH MY WIFE!

416
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:12,740
JOEY!

417
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:15,451
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA, WHOA!

418
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:17,370
HEY, I DID NOT GO OUT
WITH YOUR WIFE, OKAY?

419
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:19,288
I WENT OUT WITH HER.

420
00:17:19,288 --> 00:17:20,373
THAT'S MY WIFE!

421
00:17:21,833 --> 00:17:24,335
GET OUT!
( yelling in Russian )

422
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:26,921
WELL, WE SHOULD GO.

423
00:17:26,921 --> 00:17:27,881
YEAH.

424
00:17:30,383 --> 00:17:31,342
ROSS?

425
00:17:33,887 --> 00:17:36,138
ROSS?

426
00:17:36,138 --> 00:17:37,598
ELIZABETH.

427
00:17:40,727 --> 00:17:42,144
OKAY... OKAY...

428
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:45,189
I'M GOING TO GO
OUT THIS WINDOW.

429
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:46,607
I'LL MEET YOU AT
THE FRONT DOOR.

430
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:48,150
TELL THEM YOU'RE
GOING HOME, OKAY?

431
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:49,151
OKAY.

432
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:50,236
Rachel:
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT!

433
00:17:50,236 --> 00:17:51,320
NO, DON'T GO
IN THERE!

434
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,780
DON'T GO
IN THERE!

435
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,532
I NEED
ANOTHER SODA.

436
00:17:54,532 --> 00:17:56,409
ROSS!

437
00:17:57,785 --> 00:17:59,370
OH, MY GOD! ROSS!

438
00:17:59,370 --> 00:18:02,081
WHAT IN HEAVEN'S NAME
ARE YOU DOING HERE?

439
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:06,669
AND THAT IS WHY

440
00:18:06,669 --> 00:18:08,629
WE CANNOT SEE EACH
OTHER ANYMORE.

441
00:18:11,382 --> 00:18:12,926
ROSS...

442
00:18:12,926 --> 00:18:14,719
YOU AND I ARE GOING TO HAVE
TO HAVE A LITTLE TALK.

443
00:18:14,719 --> 00:18:16,262
DADDY, UH...
YOU'RE NEXT!

444
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:18,347
OKAY. I DIDN'T KNOW HE WAS HERE.

445
00:18:21,684 --> 00:18:23,686
LET ME JUST SEE
IF I GOT THIS STRAIGHT.

446
00:18:23,686 --> 00:18:25,855
I TELL YOU TO STAY AWAY
FROM MY DAUGHTER

447
00:18:25,855 --> 00:18:27,398
OR I'LL HAVE YOU FIRED.

448
00:18:27,398 --> 00:18:29,025
WHAT YOU HEARD WAS:

449
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:31,318
"TAKE MY DAUGHTER,
COME UP TO MY COUNTRY HOUSE

450
00:18:31,318 --> 00:18:32,987
AND RUIN MY WEEKEND
WITH RACHEL."

451
00:18:32,987 --> 00:18:34,321
OKAY, PLEASE, PLEASE, PAUL.

452
00:18:34,321 --> 00:18:35,573
JUST LET ME EXPLAIN...

453
00:18:35,573 --> 00:18:36,699
NO, LET ME EXPLAIN!

454
00:18:36,699 --> 00:18:38,701
FIRED!

455
00:18:38,701 --> 00:18:40,745
OKAY, FINE, FINE.

456
00:18:40,745 --> 00:18:42,413
HAVE ME FIRED.

457
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:46,292
BUT, UH, I WANT
YOU TO KNOW

458
00:18:46,292 --> 00:18:49,796
THAT YOU AND I ARE NOT
ALL THAT DIFFERENT.

459
00:18:49,796 --> 00:18:51,798
I MEAN...

460
00:18:51,798 --> 00:18:54,383
I, TOO, AM A NEAT GUY.

461
00:19:03,893 --> 00:19:06,353
WHAT?

462
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:08,355
AND I, TOO

463
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:11,818
AM JUST A
LOVE MACHINE.

464
00:19:14,737 --> 00:19:17,281
( humming "Love Machine" )

465
00:19:21,159 --> 00:19:23,746
( grunts )

466
00:19:31,378 --> 00:19:32,630
ROSS...

467
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:36,467
LET ME SHOW YOU
WHERE THE GUEST ROOM IS.

468
00:19:49,105 --> 00:19:50,564
I'M SO SORRY.

469
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:52,191
PLEASE STOP
FREAKING OUT.

470
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:54,234
I'M NOT FREAKING OUT.

471
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:58,572
WHY WOULD I BE FREAKING OUT?

472
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:00,867
A WOMAN NAMED HILDY CALLED
TO SAY WE WERE GETTING MARRIED

473
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:01,868
BUT THAT HAPPENS EVERY DAY.

474
00:20:01,868 --> 00:20:03,369
WAH-AHHH-AHHH!

475
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,833
HONEY, WE WERE
AT THIS BEAUTIFUL PLACE

476
00:20:08,833 --> 00:20:11,293
AND I JUST PUT OUR NAMES DOWN
FOR FUN.

477
00:20:11,293 --> 00:20:12,753
I MEAN, WHAT'S THE HARM
IN THAT?

478
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:13,921
RIGHT HERE.

479
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:16,966
( clucking )

480
00:20:16,966 --> 00:20:19,468
CHANDLER, PLEASE DON'T THINK
I WAS TRYING TO PRESSURE YOU.

481
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:20,469
PHOEBE AND RACHEL
JUST THOUGHT THAT...

482
00:20:20,469 --> 00:20:22,138
PHOEBE AND RACHEL...

483
00:20:22,138 --> 00:20:24,849
SO THE PEOPLE THAT KNEW
ABOUT OUR WEDDING BEFORE ME

484
00:20:24,849 --> 00:20:26,767
WERE YOU, PHOEBE AND RACHEL

485
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:28,435
HILDY, AND APPARENTLY
SOME BAND

486
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:30,229
CALLED THE STARLIGHT
MAGIC SEVEN

487
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:31,814
WHO ARE AVAILABLE,
BY THE WAY.

488
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:36,360
IT WAS A MISTAKE.

489
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:38,236
PLEASE DON'T TAKE THIS
TO MEAN ANYTHING

490
00:20:38,236 --> 00:20:40,198
BECAUSE IT DOESN'T.

491
00:20:42,825 --> 00:20:43,826
OKAY.

492
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:46,453
REALLY?

493
00:20:46,453 --> 00:20:48,873
YES, IF IT REALLY
DOESN'T MEAN ANYTHING

494
00:20:48,873 --> 00:20:50,583
BECAUSE YOU KNOW THAT
I'M JUST NOT READY...

495
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:54,087
I KNOW.
I KNOW.

496
00:20:54,087 --> 00:20:55,088
OKAY.

497
00:20:55,088 --> 00:20:56,714
ALL RIGHT.

498
00:20:56,714 --> 00:21:00,176
NOW I'M GOING TO GO TELL JOEY
THAT YOU'RE BACK.

499
00:21:00,176 --> 00:21:02,845
HE WAS REALLY WORRIED
ABOUT YOU.

500
00:21:08,226 --> 00:21:09,810
HEY, DID SHE BUY IT?

501
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:11,187
TOTALLY.

502
00:21:11,187 --> 00:21:12,897
SO DID HILDY SHOW YOU THE PLACE?

503
00:21:12,897 --> 00:21:15,566
YEAH, IT'S BEAUTIFUL.

504
00:21:15,566 --> 00:21:18,903
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU'RE GOING
TO ASK MONICA TO MARRY YOU.

505
00:21:18,903 --> 00:21:20,196
I KNOW.

506
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:32,583
HEY, GUNTHER.

507
00:21:32,583 --> 00:21:34,168
TAKE THESE CAPPUCCINOS
TO TABLE ELEVEN

508
00:21:34,168 --> 00:21:36,212
AND THAT GUY OVER THERE
WANTS SOME BISCOTTI.

509
00:21:36,212 --> 00:21:38,089
OH, UH, WELL, I JUST,
ACTUALLY, CAME IN

510
00:21:38,089 --> 00:21:40,382
FOR A CUP OF
COFFEE TO GO.

511
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:43,636
DO YOU STILL WORK HERE?

512
00:21:44,971 --> 00:21:48,557
NO, NO, I QUIT A LONG TIME AGO.

513
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:50,977
DID I FORGET TO TELL YOU THAT?
I'M SORRY.

514
00:21:50,977 --> 00:21:53,395
NO, THAT'S COOL.
I WAS GOING TO FIRE YOU ANYWAY.

515
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:55,397
GREAT!

